.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taur 1  "taur 0.5.0" 
.SH NAME
taur \- TAUR: an AUR\-compatible package server
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaur\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
TAUR: an AUR\-compatible package server
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
Data directory (default: $TAUR_HOME, else ~/.local/share/taur)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
taur\-serve(1)
Run the HTTP server (AUR RPC, git, snapshots, dumps, API) and optional SSH server
.TP
taur\-verify\-user(1)
Mark an account\*(Aqs email as verified (admin)
.TP
taur\-import(1)
Import a package directory containing .SRCINFO (and PKGBUILD)
.TP
taur\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.5.0
